WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.245
PESTLE scans the big forces around a market.

00:00:03.295 --> 00:00:05.049
Political and economic.

00:00:05.099 --> 00:00:07.066
Social and technological.

00:00:07.116 --> 00:00:08.964
Legal and environmental.

00:00:09.014 --> 00:00:11.986
Six forces no single brand controls.

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:14.678
Take an Australian beer brand.

00:00:14.728 --> 00:00:16.813
Younger people are drinking less.

00:00:16.863 --> 00:00:19.336
Social media is now their search engine.

00:00:19.386 --> 00:00:22.890
Ad rules are strict, and the cost of living bites.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:25.319
So the response writes itself:

00:00:25.369 --> 00:00:27.017
a premium no-alcohol range,

00:00:27.067 --> 00:00:28.361
sold through creators,

00:00:28.411 --> 00:00:30.310
inside the ad rules.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.165
Use it like this:

00:00:32.215 --> 00:00:34.464
pick the two or three forces that matter most,

00:00:34.514 --> 00:00:35.314
give a real example of each,

00:00:34.632 --> 00:00:38.542
and say what the brand should do.
